    {
      "id": "99",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 99,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "This phrase combines the nominalizer の with the な-Adjective 好き to express liking an activity (e.g., 本を読むのが好き = 'I like to read books'). の can be replaced with こと, another nominalizer. The difference is subtle: の implies a concrete or tangible action, while こと is more abstract (e.g., 本を読むことが好き implies liking the 'act of reading').",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 34,
          "slug": "のがすき",
          "title": "のがすき",
          "meaning": "Like doing, Love doing",
          "level": "JLPT5",
          "type_pascal": "GrammarPoint",
          "type_snake": "grammar_point"
        },
        "second_relatable": {
